# What must not go into the build context.
#
# Two reasons, and the second matters more. Size: node_modules is hundreds of
# megabytes that the image build re-installs from the lockfile anyway. And
# correctness: a build that copies in whatever the developer's tree happened to
# contain produces an image nobody can reproduce, which for a financial system
# means an artefact nobody can trace back to a commit.

# Version control. The image is stamped from build arguments the Makefile
# passes, so the history is not needed and its size is not wanted.
.git
.gitignore

# Build output — rebuilt inside the image, and a host binary is the wrong
# architecture as often as not.
bin/
dist/
webui/node_modules/
webui/dist/
web/dist/
node_modules/

# Local state that is not the application.
.env
*.env
!.env.example
backups/
perf/
coverage.out
coverage.html
*.prof
*.test

# Editor and platform noise.
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
.claude/

# Documentation does not change what the binary does. It is on the host and in
# the repository; the image carries the operational scripts it actually runs.
docs/
*.md
!README.md
